{%- comment -%}
  Shared markup is injected ahead of every view, so this class is defined once
  for all four layouts rather than inline in each.

  The Framework has no filter utility, and `filter` is the only way to lift a
  dark portrait's contrast before the platform dithers it. Defining it here
  keeps every view free of inline style attributes and of its own <style> block.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .sw-contrast { filter: grayscale(1) contrast(1.75) brightness(1.04); }
</style>
